      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Pain control should be a priority in cancer care. For most patients, the basic strategies are straightforward and pharmacologic: Up to 85% of cancer pain can be managed with oral agents. Barriers arise from misconceptions about opioids. The greatest single problem may be inadequate pain assessment--a deficiency that can be rectified by relying on patients to rate their pain."},
